{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\sin(x)\\cos(x)$ is the product of two, more basic, expressions: $\\sin(x)$ and $\\cos(x)$.\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ can be found using **the product rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)v(x)]\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)+u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=u'(x)v(x)+u(x)v'(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\sin(x)\\cos(x))\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\sin(x))\\cos(x)+\\sin(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\cos(x))\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The product rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\cos(x)\\cdot \\cos(x)+\\sin(x)\\cdot (-\\sin(x))\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }\\sin(x)\\text{ and }\\cos(x)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\cos^2(x)-\\sin^2(x)\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\cos^2(x)-\\sin^2(x)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=\\sin(x)\\cos(x)$.\n\n**Find $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\cos^2(x)-\\sin^2(x)$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\cos^2(x)+\\sin^2(x)$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\cos(x)-\\sin(x)$","isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$\\cos(x)+\\sin(x)$","isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
